<services>
  <!--
    Reference copy of the _service file used for the OBS package in
    SailfishOS:Chum. Upload it unchanged to the package

      harbour-ferry   -> builds rpm/harbour-ferry.spec

    <revision> points at main while a build is being iterated on. Pin it to
    the release tag (e.g. v0.3-2-release) before submitting to Chum, and bump
    it for every following release.

    Note: tar_git exports rpm/harbour-ferry.spec and rpm/harbour-ferry.changes
    next to the tarball and drops the rpm/ directory from the tarball itself.
    The build tree therefore has no spec file - which is why the spec hands
    Version and Release to qmake on the command line instead of letting
    harbour-ferry.pro read them back out of the spec.

    Note on size: the repository carries one rclone binary per architecture
    (rclone-binaries/, ~216 MB in total), all of which end up in the source
    tarball OBS keeps per revision (~75 MB compressed). The built RPM stays
    small - qmake installs only the binary matching QT_ARCH (see
    harbour-ferry.pro) and rpm compresses it to roughly 19 MB.

    ### OBS flow:
    - build package
    - Submit Package to target project: sailfishos:chum:testing (leave target package empty)
    - then it will be pushed to sailfishos:chum automatically
    - for new versions:
        - update the _service file within chum:testing
        - check build
        - submit to sailfishos:chum

  -->
  <service name="tar_git">
    <param name="url">https://github.com/Dominik-h-hub/harbour-ferry.git</param>
    <param name="branch">main</param>
    <param name="revision">main</param>
  </service>
</services>
